# Only allow file extensions supported by AWS DevOps Agent skill uploads
# Ignore all files by default
*

# Allow directories (needed for recursion)
!*/

# Allow .gitignore itself
!.gitignore

# Allowed extensions
!*.md
!*.txt
!*.json
!*.yaml
!*.yml
!*.xml
!*.csv
!*.tsv
!*.html
!*.htm
!*.png
!*.jpg
!*.jpeg
!*.gif
!*.svg
!*.webp
!*.pdf

# Re-ignore disallowed directories (must come after allowlist)
**/scripts/
**/.claude/

# Debug traces written by the skill evaluation tool and its SDK. Useful locally
# while iterating on a skill, but not part of the skill or its eval results.
**/cli_debug/
**/sdk_debug/

# Intermediate per-iteration output from functional tests. outputs/journal_records.json
# is deliberately NOT ignored — it holds the DevOps Agent journal for the run and is
# the evidence of what the evaluation actually produced. Patterns are scoped to
# outputs/ so these common filenames stay committable elsewhere under skills/.
**/outputs/classified_output.json
**/outputs/metadata.json

# Run metadata the skill evaluation tool writes at the root of each functional
# version directory. It records how the run was invoked — the region, the
# iteration count, the local skill directory — and the CloudFormation stacks the
# tool created, each named by a full stack ARN. Those ARNs carry the account the
# evaluation ran in, which is the one place an eval run names a real account that
# no redaction pass touches, because the file comes from the harness rather than
# from the agent. Nothing reads it afterwards: the evals validation check lists
# it among the files it deliberately does not look at.
#
# The path is spelled out rather than matched as **/_metadata.json so the name
# stays committable elsewhere under skills/.
**/evals/functional/*/_metadata.json
